# A recipe's render (tools/make_manual.py --renders): from P1, headphones, Pitch lock off, Scene time 0. The two high
# sines are set up before the recording (the moves take ~8 s); the clip starts on them, then strikes them.
# "# @" marks the listening times (tools/make_manual.py --times).
notips
phones 1
set 74 0
set 71 0
tapkey w0
tap PLAY
wait 2500
tap EDIT
turn K1 -40 60
turn K3 -40 60
tap HOME
tap HOME
turn K1 35 60
turn K3 36 60
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap HOME
turn K2 30 60
turn K4 30 60
wait 1500
wav bells.wav
# @ Two pure sines, high, a tritone apart (C#6 and G6), the Swell off
wait 1500
# @ Key 11 twice, bend each other, X-mod up: they ring into one metallic tone, but it never stops ringing
tapkey b10
tapkey b10
tap LFO
tap LFO
turn K4 30 80
wait 3000
# @ The cutoffs down, to about 300 Hz: the metal goes dull
tap HOME
turn K2 -24 25
turn K4 -25 25
wait 1000
# @ LFO I on Roundtooth, a cycle every 2.5 s, drone II's cutoff on it too
tap LFO
tap LFO
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
turn SELECT 29 40
tapkey b7
tapkey b7
shot bells-0.png
# @ Both cutoff sends all the way left, -100: each cycle the filters snap open and close slowly, a bell struck and ringing out
turn K2 -50 10
turn K4 -15 40
wait 12000
shot bells-1.png
wavstop
